cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Srot in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Srot: verified Indian government geodata in QGIS"
abstract: >-
  Srot brings verified Indian government geodata into QGIS, each layer carrying
  its own citation. It serves 342 ISRO Bhuvan layers across 44 states and union
  territories, the Census and Survey of India boundary sets, live data.gov.in
  feeds and OpenStreetMap presets, probing each layer before it is added so that
  empty and unavailable sources are reported rather than silently loaded.
  Publisher, licence, source URL and retrieval date are written into each layer's
  metadata, and every session exports as a runnable PyQGIS script.
type: software
